{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:9314068 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:9314068 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"9314068","source":"MED","pmid":"9314068","doi":"10.1016/s0940-2993(97)80044-9","title":"Galactosamine-induced apoptosis in the primary mouse hepatocyte cultures.","authorString":"Tsutsui S, Hirasawa K, Takeda M, Itagaki S, Kawamura S, Maeda K, Mikami T, Doi K.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Tsutsui S","firstName":"S","lastName":"Tsutsui","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedical Science, Faculty of Agriculture, University of Tokyo, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Hirasawa K","firstName":"K","lastName":"Hirasawa","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Takeda M","firstName":"M","lastName":"Takeda","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Itagaki S","firstName":"S","lastName":"Itagaki","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Kawamura S","firstName":"S","lastName":"Kawamura","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Maeda K","firstName":"K","lastName":"Maeda","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Mikami T","firstName":"T","lastName":"Mikami","initials":"T"},{"fullName":"Doi K","firstName":"K","lastName":"Doi","initials":"K"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3-4","volume":"49","journalIssueId":1077429,"dateOfPublication":"1997 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":1997,"printPublicationDate":"1997-08-01","journal":{"title":"Experimental and toxicologic pathology : official journal of the Gesellschaft fur Toxikologische Pathologie","medlineAbbreviation":"Exp Toxicol Pathol","isoabbreviation":"Exp Toxicol Pathol","nlmid":"9208920","essn":"1618-1433","issn":"0940-2993"}},"pubYear":"1997","pageInfo":"301-306","abstractText":"Galactosamine (GalN)-induced apoptosis was investigated in cultured hepatocytes from mice. The percentage of fragmented DNA measured by the ELISA method increased in a concentration-dependent manner from the very early stage, i.e. 0.5 hrs, after GalN-exposure. In addition, a ladder-like fragmentation pattern by agarose gel electrophoresis appeared first at 3 hr-exposure to 20 mM GalN, at 6 hr-exposure to 10 mM GalN and at 12 hr-exposure to 5 mM GalN, respectively. On the other hand, cytotoxicity indicated by leakage of lactate dehydrogenase from cultured hepatocytes to culture medium was first detected at 24 hrs after GalN-treatment. Morphologically, formation of blebs and apoptotic bodies was observed from 12 hr-exposure to 20 mM GalN and from 24 hr-exposure to 10 mM GalN, respectively. Thus GalN could induce apoptosis in primary hepatocyte cultures from mice.","affiliation":"Department of Biomedical Science, Faculty of Agriculture, University of Tokyo, Japan.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Liver","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Inbred C57BL"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"L-Lactate Dehydrogenase","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Galactosamine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Microscopy, Electron"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay"},{"maj